.TH DEOPJUFY-MANIFEST 5 "2026-08-21" "deopjufy 0.6.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
deopjufy-manifest \- extraction manifest, catalog, retrieval, and byte-map formats
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every directory extraction performed by
.BR deopjufy (1)
writes a deterministic
.I manifest.json
record. The manifest describes what was found, extracted, skipped, preserved as
raw bytes, left partial, rejected as unsupported, or failed.
.PP
The manifest is evidence metadata, not a whole-project compatibility grade.
Confidence describes parser evidence, not scientific accuracy. Exact byte
verification does not imply that every enclosing structure or semantic role is
known.
.SH TOP-LEVEL OBJECT
The JSON object contains these required members:
.TP
.B input
The requested path, exact byte size, SHA-256 digest, and detected type
.RB ( opj
or
.BR opju ).
.TP
.B tool
The tool name, version, and backend. The native implementation reports
.BR backend=native-parser .
.TP
.B status
One of
.BR ok ,
.BR partial ,
or
.BR unsupported .
.TP
.B items
An ordered array of artifact records.
.TP
.B warnings
An ordered array of non-fatal parser and extraction warnings.
.SH ITEM OBJECTS
Every item has a
.BR kind ,
.BR name ,
.BR status ,
and numeric
.B confidence
between 0 and 1. Missing optional fields are omitted rather than serialized as
JSON null.
.SS Status and evidence
.TP
.B status
One of
.BR extracted ,
.BR skipped ,
.BR partial ,
.BR unsupported ,
or
.BR error .
.TP
.B discovery_type, discovery_method
The evidence source, such as a parser window, parser-backed hint, object scan,
carved signature, or unknown gap.
.TP
.B heuristic
False for parser-backed evidence and true when carving, proximity, token scans,
or inferred boundaries contribute to the item.
.TP
.B extraction_method
The materialization rule. When omitted, it defaults to the discovery method.
.TP
.B completeness
Usually
.B complete
or
.BR partial .
Heuristic extracts and non-extracted items default to partial.
.TP
.B verification
One of
.BR unverified ,
.BR synthetic ,
.BR external-parity ,
or
.BR exact .
Exact means the emitted bytes or values satisfy the bounded rule represented by
that item.
.SS Identity and output
.TP
.B object_kind, content_class
Conservative object and content classifications.
.TP
.B path
The artifact path relative to the extraction root.
.TP
.B source_object_path
The best supported logical source path.
.TP
.B signature
A validated embedded format such as PNG, JPEG, GIF, SVG, or PDF.
.TP
.B rows, columns
Recovered tabular dimensions.
.TP
.B error
An explicit reason for partial, unsupported, skipped, or failed materialization.
.SS Source provenance
.TP
.B offset, length
The primary source span or carving origin.
.TP
.B range_start, range_end
An explicit half-open source range.
.TP
.B source_ranges
All source byte ranges used to derive the item.
.TP
.B decoded_length, declared_length, compression
Compression and decoded-size evidence for framed OPJU payloads.
.TP
.B family_marker, marker_offset, header_offset, stream_offset, framing_rule
Low-level framing evidence retained for decoded OPJU regions.
.TP
.B source_map_path
A sidecar mapping each recovered output byte to its source-byte offset.
.SS Semantic fields
.TP
.B structural_name
The retained wire or parser label.
.TP
.B semantic_alias
A conservative public role name supported by stated evidence. It never replaces
the structural name.
.TP
.B semantic_confidence
One of
.BR wire_exact ,
.BR corpus_high ,
.BR corpus_medium ,
or
.BR hypothesis .
This rates the alias separately from byte verification.
.TP
.B preview_status
.B present
or
.BR absent ,
independent from graph-definition support and artifact-write status.
.TP
.B embedded_payload
Whether named attachment content is physically embedded. An external workbook
reference uses false.
.SH EXTRACTION PROFILES
.TP
.B --human
Keep human-facing primary artifacts and omit low-level machine recovery output.
This is the default profile.
.TP
.B --human-only
Skip unknown-region raw and text output.
.TP
.B --human-artifacts-only
Skip unknown-region output and machine-oriented provenance sidecars.
.TP
.B --extended
Include decoded-payload indexes, source maps, raw and carved-text regions,
analysis fields, and other machine-oriented provenance.
.TP
.B --map
Include extended output plus a complete reconstructable byte map.
.TP
.B --parser-only
Restrict discovery and collection to parser-backed candidates. This option is
independent of the output profile.
.SH OUTPUT LAYOUT
Applicable artifacts use stable sanitized paths below the selected output root:
.EX
manifest.json
tables/
matrices/
notes/
images/
attachments/
functions/
analyses/
metadata/
provenance/
raw/
byte-map/
.EE
.PP
Not every directory is created. Original logical names remain in the manifest
when filesystem names require sanitization.
.SH SEMANTIC PROVENANCE
OPJU runs emit a canonical semantic index when qualifying evidence exists. The
index can describe exact descriptor-owned worksheet symbols, aliases, metadata,
formulas, report-cell paths, calculation fields and UIDs, uniquely resolved
range references, report-grid state, persistent graph source slots, and explicit
unresolved or ambiguous relationships.
.PP
Semantic links resolve only from bounded parser evidence. Long-name similarity
does not create ownership. Missing equations and unresolved graph or dataset
owners remain explicit.
.PP
Exactly resolved MSer-backed report-reference tables expose readable values and
retain an offset sidecar. A table is promoted only when every integer resolves
uniquely within one complete source string set.
.SH BYTE MAP
.B extract --map
writes
.IR byte-map/index.json .
Its ordered, non-overlapping segments partition the complete interval from zero
through the exact input size. Concatenating segment files reconstructs the input,
and both source and reconstructed SHA-256 values are recorded.
.PP
Segment classes describe evidence boundaries such as parser-bounded, carved,
heuristic, or unknown. A complete byte map proves preservation of every byte,
not semantic decoding of every byte.
.SH CATALOG FORMAT
.B list --json
uses schema version 1. The top level contains
.BR schema_version ,
.BR document ,
.BR tool ,
command and parser status, warnings, evidence fields, and
.BR items .
.PP
Each catalog item adds an opaque
.B item:v1:
ID, a list of
.BR retrieval_formats ,
and an optional
.B parent_id
when exact source paths prove one immediate parent. IDs are deterministic for
unchanged input bytes but are document-bound and must not be parsed.
.SH RETRIEVAL FORMAT
.B get FILE ITEM_ID --json
rebuilds the exhaustive catalog, validates the ID, and materializes only the
selected object through the canonical extractor path. Schema version 1 contains
.BR document ,
.BR tool ,
.BR item ,
.BR status ,
.BR artifacts ,
and
.BR warnings .
.PP
Inline primary content uses
.B content_encoding
equal to
.BR json ,
.BR text ,
or
.BR base64 .
Tabular file output supports CSV, TSV, JSONL, and optional XLSX. Image formats are
advertised only for validated recovered media or an exact parser-linked page
preview. Unsupported materializers return an explicit partial response.
.SH DETERMINISM
Manifest items are sorted by path, kind, and name. Output paths remain relative.
Unknown fields are additive; missing optional fields are omitted. Parser-backed
and heuristic evidence remain distinguishable. No command silently replaces an
unsupported parser result with guessed content.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deopjufy (1),
.BR deopjufy-view (1),
.BR deopjufy-formats (7)
